  "limitations": [
    "A hypothesis from a simplified spectral negative-to-print model; not a measured reproduction of real Gold200 at box speed versus two stops extra exposure.",
    "Upstream profile data include processed manufacturer curves and modeled dye behavior; this local pipeline omits masking-coupler chemistry, grain, halation and spatial effects, and uses a linear-sRGB spectral basis.",
    "The starting camera Standard JPEG has already rendered tone, white balance and clipping. Its fitted inverse estimates scene RGB; missing highlight or shadow information cannot be recovered.",
    "Stock curves, modeled interlayer amount, print paper, baseline filtration and D55 scene illuminant are held fixed. This does not simulate push/pull development or a scanner auto-balance.",
    "Scalar print-gain compensation is an optical-model exposure control; chromatic filtration is mathematically fixed but is not a physical enlarger spectral-filter implementation.",
    "Baseline and candidate previews use unquantized GR3X_CAMERA SlotParams. No firmware was installed, built, written or optically measured; actual-camera transfer remains unverified.",
    "The 33^3 exported targets and preview grids are trilinearly interpolated; finite-grid interpolation slightly changes the exact continuous middle-gray result.",
    "The fit cannot reproduce every 3D spectral response. Each error is measured against its own different target: independent synthetic p95 is 5.228 baseline and 3.450 candidate, while full 33^3 cube p95 is 18.5551 baseline and 19.6846 candidate; maxima are 33.6747 and 42.1978 ΔE00. Saturated and extreme RGB regions can depart severely from the target despite modest common-photo errors.",
    "The photographic fit-error decrease 1.019 to 0.942 ΔE00 is a representability comparison between different targets. It does not measure aesthetic quality or establish a preference for the +2 EV result."
  ],
